  "critical_dimension_theorem": "Let M be a compact connected smooth d-manifold without boundary,with positive continuous volume density,and Z:M->C^q a C1 map,q>=2,satisfying the ENTIRE actual-conjugate moment law integral Z^alpha barZ^beta=delta_(alpha,beta)rho_|alpha| alpha!,rho0=1. Its compact pushforward is U(q)-invariant by the polarized moment kernel and polynomial approximation,and its support is exactly Z(M). For d<=2q-1,variable norm would force an open annulus in a lower-dimensional Lipschitz image,impossible. A nonzero tuple requires d>=2q-1. At critical d=2q-1,normR is constant,rho_m=R^(2m)/(q)_m,and Z pushes positive source volume to uniform sphere area. Any equal-dimensional C1 positive-volume-preserving map is a finite cover:at a rank-deficient point the image of an epsilon-ball has target mass o(epsilon^d),contradicting source mass>=c epsilon^d. Thus Z is a sphere covering,and since q>=2 it is one-sheeted and M is C1-diffeomorphic to S^(2q-1). No analogous conclusion in higher source dimension,for signed/holomorphic-only moments,or for q1 nontrivial circle covers. The theorem is an all-order geometric proof,not finite-sample inference.",
  "finite_quotient_exclusion": "For EVERY nontrivial finite subgroup Gamma of SU2,the full compact core M=SU2/Gamma is a smooth positive-Haar three-manifold with pi1=Gamma. GRADIALCRITDIM20261116,q2,therefore excludes EVERY nonzero C1 pair A,B with full phase-balanced factorial radial law h(A^r barA^s B^u barB^v)=delta_rs delta_uv rho_(r+u)r!u!,for ANY rho. In particular no nonlinear regular coordinate choice in ANY matrix-entry degree on either ACTUAL SL2/2O or SL2/2I realizes this law,even without equivariance or a selected representation. This blocks the two-coordinate factorial-radial specialization of Lius newly audited coherent-state circuit on all nontrivial finite right quotients. It does NOT exclude arbitrary phase-invariant tables satisfying only the circuits alternating equations,arbitrary four-term phases,or general pure unsafe phases. The retained Gaussian radial bridge is unaffected:it is homogenization in FOUR ambient Gaussian variables,not such a quotient coordinate pair. Gamma1 standard sphere coordinates remain a positive control;the SO3 rank-one circuit uses a different law. Both full exceptional MZ decisions remainOPEN.",
